# Negative fixture: wtest_map_test runs bin/wtest_map_check on this file
# with expect_fail — it guards the checker itself. A checker that stopped
# failing would silently pass every selection regression, so this pins
# the failure path end-to-end: docs/todo.txt selects nothing, therefore
# the expect below must produce a 'wtest_map_check: FAIL' and exit 1.
# The real expectations live in tests/wtest/map_expectations.expect.
case docs/todo.txt
expect win64_hello_test

# The -f order hint (tools/wtest_map_check.w header;
# ai_tooling_next_steps.md 2026-07-29 U5 incident):
# tests/wtest/manifest_order_fail.json lists two eternal real build.json
# targets (tests, wv2) in the OPPOSITE of build.json's relative order,
# so the implicit order property must fail — and, because the case
# carries '-f', the FAIL detail must name the fixture manifest and the
# "-f fixture manifests must mirror build.json's relative order (or add
# 'noorder')" rule (asserted by wtest_map_test's expect_stderr in
# build.base.json). The expects themselves hold; only the order
# property fails.
case -f tests/wtest/manifest_order_fail.json widget/order.dat
expect wv2
expect tests
